    <item>
      <title>Browser Use 1.0 deletes 80% of its library - the agent now writes Python straight to Chrome over CDP, scoring up to 33 points higher at 2.7-5.2x lower cost</title>
      <link>https://news.sulat.com/2026/11/10/browser-use-1-0-cdp-python-repl-rewrite/</link>
      <guid isPermaLink="true">https://news.sulat.com/2026/11/10/browser-use-1-0-cdp-python-repl-rewrite/</guid>
      <pubDate>Tue, 10 Nov 2026 01:00:00 -0800</pubDate>
      <category>AI &amp; Agents</category>
      <description><![CDATA[<p><img src="https://news.sulat.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/browser-use-1-0-banner.jpg" alt="Browser Use 1.0 release banner" style="max-width:100%"/></p>
<p><b>'No DOM serializer, no action schema, nothing in between.' Defaults now route to Browser Use's cloud and gateway model; the docs warn model-written code runs as you, so containerize untrusted tasks.</b></p>
<blockquote>&ldquo;Predefined state and action space make it worse.&rdquo; - <a href="https://news.sulat.com/2026/11/10/browser-use-1-0-cdp-python-repl-rewrite/">Browser Use, on X, launching 1.0</a></blockquote>
<blockquote>&ldquo;An action space is what made a run replayable; a program step gives you effects instead of a diff.&rdquo; - <a href="https://news.sulat.com/2026/11/10/browser-use-1-0-cdp-python-repl-rewrite/">John Rood, on the trade-off, replying to Zunic</a></blockquote>
<p>Sources: <a href="https://news.sulat.com/2026/11/10/browser-use-1-0-cdp-python-repl-rewrite/">Sulat AI &amp; Tech News</a></p>
<p>Feedback: <a href="sms:+16506139572?&amp;body=Digest%2011/10%3A%20loved%20%22Browser%20Use%201.0%20deletes%2080%25%20of%20its%20libr...%22">Loved it</a> &middot; <a href="sms:+16506139572?&amp;body=Digest%2011/10%3A%20meh%20on%20%22Browser%20Use%201.0%20deletes%2080%25%20of%20its%20libr...%22">Meh</a> &middot; <a href="sms:+16506139572?&amp;body=Digest%2011/10%3A%20less%20like%20%22Browser%20Use%201.0%20deletes%2080%25%20of%20its%20libr...%22">Less of this</a> &middot; <a href="sms:+16506139572?&amp;body=https%3A//news.sulat.com/2026/11/10/browser-use-1-0-cdp-python-repl-rewrite/%0A">Chat about it</a></p>]]></description>
